<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
        The PAYMENTS emission tables, in dcre_pay. PRW is their single writer (R-04).

        THE ONE STRUCTURAL DIFFERENCE FROM CRW, and the reason this is a fork rather
        than a rename: there is no run_date column anywhere below.

        CRW carries run_date in every business key because collections WAREHOUSES.
        CDE estimates a collection day per transaction, CRW emits only the slice whose
        process_date equals the run date, and the futured remainder legitimately
        becomes due AGAIN on a later run date as a NEW physical artifact. run_date is
        what keeps those artifacts distinct.

        Payments has no CDE, no cde_schedule row and no collection day: a payment is
        processed immediately (Sean, 2026-08-07). An arrival is emitted once, in full,
        by the PRW stage AGT launches after PAI. There is no futured remainder, so
        there is no second run date, so run_date is not part of any identity here.
        Carrying it would be worse than redundant: a nullable-or-defaulted date in a
        unique constraint is an identity dimension that varies for reasons unrelated
        to the business entity, which is precisely how an idempotency key stops
        matching itself across a restart.

        What that removes, concretely: crw_emission_group's (arrival_id, run_date)
        becomes (arrival_id); crw_emission's (arrival_id, run_date, batch_ordinal)
        becomes (arrival_id, batch_ordinal); and CRW's countPriorArtifacts, which
        enumerates a parent's artifacts across OTHER run dates so a re-emission never
        reuses an outbound MsgId, has nothing to count and is gone.

        What it does NOT remove: the group/batch SPLIT. That is a Fintegrate file-size
        cap (SCRUM-55, max tx per outbound pain.008), not warehousing machinery, and a
        300k-transaction payment arrival needs it exactly as much as a collections one.
        The design's wording is "MINUS the warehousing columns", and run_date is the
        warehousing column.

        Re-run safety uses onFail="CONTINUE", never MARK_RAN (A-79, A-81). MARK_RAN
        records the skip PERMANENTLY, so a database that was merely not-yet-ready at
        the moment of the check never gets the change at all. That shape has already
        cost this project two defects, one of them a silent permanent hang.
    -->
    <changeSet id="prw-001-emission-group" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="CONTINUE">
            <not><tableExists tableName="prw_emission_group"/></not>
        </preConditions>
        <createTable tableName="prw_emission_group">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="arrival_id" type="UUID"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <!-- VARCHAR(16), the width of the authority (A-43, ruled 2026-08-08): this column
                 carries tx_header.client_token, falling back to initg_pty only when no R-31
                 filename token existed. 35 was initg_pty's pain.008 width and was inherited
                 from a source this column no longer has; 16 matches client_token,
                 crw_emission_group.client, ext_tx_status.client and prg_watermark.client, which
                 is the set of columns that must join to it. -->
            <column name="client" type="VARCHAR(16)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="source_msg_id" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="applied_max" type="INT"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="total_tx" type="BIGINT"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="total_amount" type="DECIMAL(18,2)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="expected_batch_count" type="INT"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="split" type="BOOLEAN"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <!-- BaseEntity (configuration.md point 20). -->
            <column name="version" type="BIGINT" defaultValueNumeric="0">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="created_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="updated_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
        <rollback>
            <dropTable tableName="prw_emission_group"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- The plan claim's idempotency key. ONE plan per arrival: CRW's key is
         (arrival_id, run_date) because the same parent replans on a later date;
         here the arrival IS the identity.

         client + source_msg_id is the SECOND uniqueness tuple and is kept, not
         folded away: it is the business identity of the inbound instruction book
         as the client stated it, and it is what catches a redelivered file that
         was assigned a fresh arrival_id upstream. Dropping it because arrival_id
         is "already unique" would narrow the key below the full business identity,
         which is the failure this estate has paid for twice. -->
    <changeSet id="prw-001-emission-group-identity" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="CONTINUE">
            <not>
                <indexExists tableName="prw_emission_group" indexName="uq_prw_group_arrival"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="prw_emission_group" columnNames="arrival_id"
                             constraintName="uq_prw_group_arrival"/>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="prw_emission_group" columnNames="client, source_msg_id"
                             constraintName="uq_prw_group_client_msg"/>
        <rollback>
            <dropUniqueConstraint tableName="prw_emission_group"
                                  constraintName="uq_prw_group_client_msg"/>
            <dropUniqueConstraint tableName="prw_emission_group"
                                  constraintName="uq_prw_group_arrival"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="prw-001-emission" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="CONTINUE">
            <not><tableExists tableName="prw_emission"/></not>
        </preConditions>
        <createTable tableName="prw_emission">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="group_id" type="UUID"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="arrival_id" type="UUID"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="batch_ordinal" type="INT"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="outbound_msg_id" type="VARCHAR(64)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="file_name" type="VARCHAR(128)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <!-- PLANNED -> MATERIALIZED -> VISIBLE, born at CRW's post-widening
                 VARCHAR(32) rather than at the VARCHAR(16) it had to be ALTERed from. -->
            <column name="state" type="VARCHAR(32)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="tx_count" type="BIGINT"/>
            <column name="control_sum" type="DECIMAL(18,2)"/>
            <column name="visible_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ"/>
            <!-- BaseEntity (configuration.md point 20). -->
            <column name="version" type="BIGINT" defaultValueNumeric="0">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="created_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="updated_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
        <rollback>
            <dropTable tableName="prw_emission"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- The batch claim's idempotency key: the FULL identity of ONE physical
         outbound artifact. CRDB's UPSERT resolves on the PRIMARY KEY only, so the
         writer's INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (arrival_id, batch_ordinal) needs this
         constraint to exist or a restarted stage duplicates instead of no-opping.

         uq_prw_emission_outbound_msg is the cross-ARRIVAL guard and is the reason
         the ordinal key is safe to narrow from CRW's three columns to two: an
         outbound MsgId that repeated for any reason would be a duplicate on the
         wire, and it fails here at the claim rather than at Fintegrate. -->
    <changeSet id="prw-001-emission-identity" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="CONTINUE">
            <not>
                <indexExists tableName="prw_emission" indexName="uq_prw_emission_arrival_ordinal"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="prw_emission" columnNames="arrival_id, batch_ordinal"
                             constraintName="uq_prw_emission_arrival_ordinal"/>
        <createIndex tableName="prw_emission" indexName="uq_prw_emission_outbound_msg" unique="true">
            <column name="outbound_msg_id"/>
        </createIndex>
        <rollback>
            <dropIndex tableName="prw_emission" indexName="uq_prw_emission_outbound_msg"/>
            <dropUniqueConstraint tableName="prw_emission"
                                  constraintName="uq_prw_emission_arrival_ordinal"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="prw-001-emission-member" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="CONTINUE">
            <not><tableExists tableName="prw_emission_member"/></not>
        </preConditions>
        <createTable tableName="prw_emission_member">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="emission_id" type="UUID"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="sequence" type="INT"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="e2e" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="amount" type="DECIMAL(18,2)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <!-- BaseEntity (configuration.md point 20). -->
            <column name="version" type="BIGINT" defaultValueNumeric="0">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="created_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="updated_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
        <rollback>
            <dropTable tableName="prw_emission_member"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- The member claim is set-based and re-runnable, so it needs the conflict
         target to exist: ON CONFLICT (emission_id, sequence) DO NOTHING. -->
    <changeSet id="prw-001-emission-member-identity" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="CONTINUE">
            <not>
                <indexExists tableName="prw_emission_member"
                             indexName="uq_prw_member_emission_sequence"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="prw_emission_member" columnNames="emission_id, sequence"
                             constraintName="uq_prw_member_emission_sequence"/>
        <rollback>
            <dropUniqueConstraint tableName="prw_emission_member"
                                  constraintName="uq_prw_member_emission_sequence"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
